From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 9 Jun 2026 06:09:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00980/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for OWED from .365:
 latent-register augmentation for the 11 HIDDEN-STATE games. The determinism
 probe (results/arc3_determinism_probe.json) found 11/25 games where the
 visible grid does NOT determine the dynamics (same frame_hash + action ->
 different next grid). Augment the state with inferred latent boolean
 registers (counter / collected-flag / phase) so the augmented state becomes
 Markov, and measure: does the induced model's consistency energy DROP on the
 hidden-state games vs the grid-only baseline? This is the named
 direction-killer (a grid->grid model is under-determined on hidden state);
 CASSANDRA (arXiv:2601.18620) corroborates programmatic+stochastic world
 modeling for exactly this regime.

Co-Authored-By: Gemini CLI <noreply@google.com>
